  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence to exploit. The most critical uncertainty is establishing a performance baseline before testing more complex configurations. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most interpretable configuration: it uses a standard linear encoder (PCA), avoids aggregation and fusion complexity, and isolates the RNA signal. This gives a clean reference point to determine whether (a) image modality adds value, (b) multimodal fusion outperforms either single modality, and (c) more complex encoders (scvi, scgpt) or aggregation strategies (transformer) provide meaningful gains over this simple baseline. Starting here maximizes interpretability of all subsequent comparisons and ensures that any performance improvement in later experiments can be attributed to specific design choices rather than confounded by multiple simultaneous changes."
